===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{surname|en|English and [[Irish]]|from=patronymics}}.
# {{given name|en|female|from=Celtic languages}}, associated by [[folk etymology]] with {{m|en|joy}} and {{m|en|rejoice}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1860|author=Mrs Henry Wood (Ellen Wood)|title=East Lynne
|passage="It's a curious name," remarked Captain Levison. "'''Joyce''' - '''Joyce'''! I never heard such a name. Is it a Christian name or a surname?"<br>"She was baptised '''Joyce'''. It is not so very uncommon. Her name is '''Joyce''' Hallijohn. She has been with us several years."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1959|author=Anne Sexton|title= The Double Image
|passage=You call me ''mother'', and I remember my mother again,<br>somewhere in greater Boston, dying.<br>I remember we named you '''Joyce'''<br>so we could call you Joy.}}
# {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Clallam County|s/Washington|c/USA}}, named after founder Joseph M. Joyce. 

